SETTING-UP YOUR ENVIRONMENT

Use the appropriate script from the setup directory.
The setup script expects two arguments: The top-level source code directory for the VALOR/DUNE and VALOR/FMWK packages.

Example:
% source setup/setup_at_XYZ.sh /path/to/dune/top/level/dir /path/to/fmwk/top/level/dir 

BUILDING THE VALOR CODE

% cd /path/to/dune/nuosc/top/level/dir
% ./configure --help
% ./configure <specify options or no options, autodetection of paths possible>
% make

RUNNING THE ANALYSIS CODE:

To run the VALOR/DUNE analysis ROOT macros, use `valor_dune' instead of `root'.
The valor_dune application is ROOT with all the VALOR/DUNE and VALOR/FMWK libraries loaded.
When running a VALO macro: 
% valor_dune 'macros/dir/some_script.C("/some/path/some/file.root",some_number)'
make sure there are NO spaces within ''.

